            <div xml:id="d519">

                <pb facs="0618" n="550" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg550"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851.857 Su 8/83½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">17 April, 1916</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: Thank you for letting me
                    see this statement of fact which is to accompany our communication to the
                    Imperial German Government. It seems to me quite complete enough.</p>
                <p>I understood you to say that the affidavits received by mail will necessitate
                    only one or two alterations of detail in the statement.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
